A||||15||FieroRacer||Close encounter of the piggy kind||||6||
Z||000000||FieroRacer||10-01-2001||12:26 AM||||I was driving the nova to pick up a friend late for work this evening.  On our way to his job, we were going 80mph in a residential area down a two lane (one for each direction) road with no intersections.  All of a sudden I fly past a cop going the other way.  I saw him hit his brakes and prepare to turn.  Told my friend to hold on, swung the car into a side street causing the engine to cut out.  I stuck that old girl into neutral as the cop went flying by lights a blasting.  Fired the nova back up and drove off (though a lot more slowly).||||reg||6
Z||000001||Tonker||10-01-2001||12:33 AM||||LOL, quick thinking.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||fierohoho||10-01-2001||04:06 AM||||There you are, pull this post over son, we need to talk <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>'84 SE 2.5l<BR>'85 Coupe 2.5l now getting a 3800<BR>'86 SE 2.5l<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/lightbar.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||loafer87gt||10-01-2001||11:39 AM||||Speaking of pigs, I'll share my buddies plight with you. Him and his Dad decided to get a 100 head of ferral pigs for their farm. About a week after they got them, they broke loose through the fence and have been terrorizing  all the people in my old home town. Its kinda funny whenever I go home because it seem like you see them everywhere. I even saw one up on top of a round bale outside of our farm. LAst week, I guess our local taxidermerist got chased by a pack of them. Everyone has now been giving the OK to hunt the pigs to get rid of them, so its a toss up which is more amusing, the pigs, or the halftonnes filled with rednecks brandishing firearms chasing them. The whole thing kinda reminds me of that south park episode where the chickens get loose and raise hell around town.||||reg||1
Z||000004||gargoyle||10-01-2001||12:49 PM||||I had my own close encounter this weekend at the F1 race at Indy. I was sitting waiting for the light to turn green and there was this ricer sitting next to me. Well the light change and he sort of got on it and I thought, what the heck and punched it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Now I was in the left lane and as soon as I grabbed second I shut it down and turned left into a Home Depot after waiting for traffic. I didn't know it but it wasn't open yet so I just started to turn around when I saw THREE State Troopers, lights and sirens blazing   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> go up the street at a very high rate of speed. When I pulled back out( going the other way now) I noticed they had stopped somebody about 2 blocks up the street. As I looked to my left I saw TWO more Troopers sitting in the gas station at the corner we had just roared by.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> The good thing is I got out of it and turned, his problem was he kept his foot in it and just kept accelerating. I think they got him. Can you imagine being pulled over by three squads. I just left the area counting my blessing and was a very good boy the rest of the weekend.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> <p>[This message has been edited by gargoyle (edited 10-01-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fogglethorpe||10-01-2001||04:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroRacer:<BR><B>I was driving the nova to pick up a friend late for work this evening.  On our way to his job, we were going 80mph in a residential area down a two lane (one for each direction) road with no intersections.  All of a sudden I fly past a cop going the other way.  I saw him hit his brakes and prepare to turn.  Told my friend to hold on, swung the car into a side street causing the engine to cut out.  I stuck that old girl into neutral as the cop went flying by lights a blasting.  Fired the nova back up and drove off (though a lot more slowly).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You drive 80mph down a residential street? I'd say it's you, and not the member of your local constabulary, that is a pig.<BR>Have a beautiful day.<BR>................<BR>Oink! <P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||fierospeeder||10-01-2001||04:57 PM||||Ive done this twice, but i cant say for sure they were out to get me.<P>Once was in my fiero.  On ogden aka route 66 coming back from school  Theres a single lane  section where it curves around a bridge,  I love going 60 around the curves.  Im not going to kill anyone except myself.  Remember its single road.  I was about 2-4 blocks away when i see flashing lights behind me, was a cop.  I quickly turn left into a side street doing several turns on the side streets.   All i can say is i didn't get pulled over.  <P>Another was, im on my motorcycle.  Im going about 60-?  over a large 4 lane bridge.  While im on top, i suddenly pass a state trooper, i believe.  Im not sure if he turned around, but the first side street i pulled into and took my time getting lost.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Kasdan||10-01-2001||07:58 PM||||Mine was...i passed a cop doing 70 in a 55...he pulls me over.. <P>Cop:  Isnt this one of those old Fiero GT's?<BR>me:  Yep, just got it.<BR>Cop:  Know how fast you were going?<BR>me: Want the truth or a joke?<BR>Cop: Lets go with the joke first. im having a good day (good thing to hear)<BR>So i proceed to tell him a joke, which if you really want to know what iot was ill tell you if you email me<BR>Cop:  hah, thats a good one!  well, since i used to own one of these babies ill let ya know, i know how fun they are to drive.<P>Lets just say i got off easy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero21.jpg">         <BR>Power Steering, Holley Scoop<BR>Aim=FieroDriver1986||||reg||1
Z||000008||Formula88||10-01-2001||11:06 PM||||The best evasive I ever did was in 1983 in an '81 Buick Skylark with it's carbureated Iron Duke! I'm heading down Six Forks Rd. at about 65 (in a 45) when I pass a cop going the other way.  He turns around, and I nail it.  I'm flying down to the intersection at Wake Forest Rd. and go screeching around the corner, when I see a Sheriff's Deputy sitting at the light (oh, boy!).  So I'm going down Wake Forest Rd. knowing I have no chance in hell of outrunning them, so as I come up to Al Smith Buick, I pull in and park between two other silver 4 door Buick Skylarks, get out and walk up to McDonald's for a few hours.  They flew by and never looked.  If traffic hadn't slowed them down to where they couldn't see me turn into the dealership, I would have been toast.<P>The funny punchline came as I'm walking back to the car.  A salesman swoops down to make his pitch as I walk up to the car, get in, and drive off.  He thought I was stealing it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Then he noticed I had tags.  Luckily it didn't occur to him to note the number.||||reg||1
Z||000009||My7Fieros||10-01-2001||11:20 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fogglethorpe:<BR><B> You drive 80mph down a residential street? I'd say it's you, and not the member of your local constabulary, that is a pig.<BR>Have a beautiful day.<BR>................<BR>Oink! <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Well said fogglethorpe...I was wondering if anybody else noticed that. Watch the "pig" name calling, boy.......you're new to this foruma and there <I>are</I> members on here that are cops...such as fierohoho and <B>myself</B>. If I'd caught ya going 80 on a two lane residential road, I would've locked your ass up.<P><P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000010||GarethWright||10-02-2001||01:46 AM||||I got to see my neighborhood on one of those police shows, but only for a split second, some drunk was speeding in Bixby (next town over), came down a street 2 miles from me(91st) and turned on to Garnett (street my neighborhood opens on to), after another few miles, he crashes into a ditch in front of the Burger King I used to go to lunch at in High School.<BR>The tape was from back in '93, so I wasn't in this neighborhood at the time, but still interesting.||||reg||1
Z||000011||artherd||10-02-2001||07:12 AM||||Hrm, 80 in a residential area inside a city limits?<P>I mean, it's one thing to be crusing in the middle of a 4-lane (each way) freeway at the speeds our cars (if well maintained) are designed for...  <P>But do 80 past my house and I'd call the cops on you myself.<P>Oink ;0)<P>Clever piece of evasion though.  Also liked the one about pulling into the dealership, hah!<P>Just don't go that fast in a nova on a 2lane residential street, yeikes!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroRacer:<BR><B>I was driving the nova to pick up a friend late for work this evening.  On our way to his job, we were going 80mph in a residential area down a two lane (one for each direction) road with no intersections.  All of a sudden I fly past a cop going the other way.  I saw him hit his brakes and prepare to turn.  Told my friend to hold on, swung the car into a side street causing the engine to cut out.  I stuck that old girl into neutral as the cop went flying by lights a blasting.  Fired the nova back up and drove off (though a lot more slowly).</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||1
Z||000012||Gerald||10-02-2001||05:52 PM||||Ohhh Chase stories. Goodie. Well heres the best one I got but Im still young so there will be better ones in the future im sure. But anyhow Im in my 87 Fiero coupe that I had been driving for only a month at the time. Im heading to Edmonton on hiway 2 with my friend behind me in his 90 Dodge Shadow ES. So I start showing off to the turbo dodge boy and star weaving traffic at about 90 mph. After about 20 secs of this my cell rings and my friend who is despretly trying to keep up asks me If I saw the cop that crossed the meridian with his lights on. So I told him to take the next exit and hung up the phone. I ended up heading to Ponoka as I saw the cherries on the overpass in my rearview. Laughed my ass off. Tool a leak. Swaped CDs and still made it to Edmonton in record time.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||EdsB52||10-03-2001||12:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by loafer87gt:<BR><B>Speaking of pigs, I'll share my buddies plight with you. Him and his Dad decided to get a 100 head of ferral pigs for their farm. About a week after they got them, they broke loose through the fence and have been terrorizing  all the people in my old home town. Its kinda funny whenever I go home because it seem like you see them everywhere. I even saw one up on top of a round bale outside of our farm. LAst week, I guess our local taxidermerist got chased by a pack of them. Everyone has now been giving the OK to hunt the pigs to get rid of them, so its a toss up which is more amusing, the pigs, or the halftonnes filled with rednecks brandishing firearms chasing them. The whole thing kinda reminds me of that south park episode where the chickens get loose and raise hell around town.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sounds like something out of the movie, "Deliverance."||||reg||1
Z||000014||Leadfoot||10-03-2001||01:08 AM||||I had a close encounter with my bro-in-law (mike) several years ago.  We were doing 85 in a 45 at one in the morning in my mike's old impala cop car.  We just reached the top of this hill that was about 3 miles from his home when I see on the side of the road a car that just hit the brake lights.  As we whizzed pasted it I noticed it was a copper.  I was waiting for Mike to slow down and pull over but he just kept right on trucking.  I said "what are you doing?" He replied, "the way I figure it, by the time he catches up we'll be home already."  I chuckled but kept looking nervously in mirror to see if the cop was on our tail.  Well we finally reached the road that lead to his home and parked the car in the driveway (which is a block away from the main road).  As we got out of the car all we hear is the sound of sirens slowly fading away.  Poor cop was still thinking he was hot on tracks.  Ah to be a teenager again.      ||||reg||1
Z||000015||EdsB52||10-03-2001||01:09 AM||||This last weekend I went out to my car at about 9pm to find the coldesac in which I live, fully congested with parked cars. So I knew my fnckin a$$hole neighbors were at it again. They hold parties till all hours of the night and plug the coldesac, but never like this before. So I get in my camaro and make my neighbor aware of what kind of an a$$hole he is with high audibility. As he's moving one of the cars and appologizing, I squeek by and lay down the pedal. I lay down 50+ feet of scratch and then grab second and cherp 'em again. By then I'm going about 50 and the intersection is quickly approaching. As I come to the intersection, a female cop is there in response to one of my good neighbors complaining about the one bad neighbor we have. So at this point I think I'm hosed, but she actually lets me go, as I related to her I was pissed because that one neighbor often pulls this sh!t and now they've gone over the edge. She could have racked me for several citations, but did not.||||reg||1
